    spawn_trail.js)    echo "  THE TRAIL OUTLIVED THE BOOT IT BELONGS TO. checkBoot must compare the boot id on EVERY frame, not once per page load - against the STORED id on the first frame and the LIVE id after that. It is the only clear that can land on the frame REPORTING the new boot, which is the only clear that also wipes a stale fix pushed in between: the old link keeps ticking at 4 Hz and its next frame lands ~160 ms AFTER the spawn command, so a pre-emptive clearTrack() leaves exactly two points and the chart strokes a 5 km line between the placement the operator abandoned and the one they chose. Watch for: \`if(bootChecked) return\` coming back; the comparison reverting to savedBootId on every frame; a clear on every frame instead of on a CHANGE (that silently deletes the trail as it is drawn - checks 5-7 are the acceptance case); doSpawn clearing ABOVE its ok gate again, which costs the operator the trail and the drawn route on a REFUSED spawn; a bare \`track = []\` returning to resetForNewArea, which leaves the localStorage mirror and the armed save alive to write it back. This suite is worthless without home_spawn.py checks 6b and 7 - an accepted spawn mints a new boot_id, a refused one does not (checkBoot / clearTrack / doSpawn / resetForNewArea in static/asv.html)." ;;
