koWithAis at the standoff, runRoute spliced, the ladder settling) - and the held bar's ROUTE ROUND HER NOW is the same press. If 14-14d went red with 17 green, a world lifting aisAroundTick has not learned aisAroundGo. AND 17h: held on a TURN (no mark) the way round picks the plan up at its NEXT waypoint routed round her, and the bar says she was stopped on a turn - never a promise of a line she is not on AND 18-18i (2026-09-28, THE TREADMILL): the override STANDS through a clear frame and adopts the hazard's name (guardOverrideOk / guardHazardKey), is ended by a different hazard (said, both named), by the release (behind her), by a stale press that met no hazard in 45 s, or by a contact UNDER WAY closing 5 m nearer - never by a parked hazard passed; CONTINUE AT LOW keeps the bar up with RELEASE LOW while the counterfactual at the plan's speed reads SLOW (asked whoever holds the throttle); released, the note says 'still at LOW on your authority' and the bar stands as LOW - OPERATOR'S AUTHORITY; releaseLow frees the latch and logs it; CANCEL OVERRIDE releases it too. AND 19-19i (2026-09-28, THE TIGHTER WAY ROUND): only HER - the contact routed round, by MMSI or else the first one the line ahead runs into (aisHerPoly) - gets a ring (aisRoundKeepout: a ship-length from her center, the standoff plus the buffer from her hull); every other contact is the guard's bare hull (a contact 32 m off the far end must not push the rejoin); a second hull on the line inside the hold horizon puts the rejoin past both; the way in is the TAUT path round her ring (tautRoundHer), the router asked only where walls block both sides; in a set the rejoin is hull + buffer + standoff; the shorter side; the held way in judged at the standoff. 14b-17h re-pinned: the rejoin at e = 65 for the 30 m workboat (it was 80). AND 20-20h (2026-09-28, FRIGGA): the ladder's frame BETWEEN the way round's upload and its Start (onReply) reads the paused boat's drift as HOLD and posts nothing - heldResumeOwns st